<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>
    <!--
      The pre-Compose window background, light. Must track SwipeyLightColors.canvas in
      ui/design/Tokens.kt — the two are the same surface, a few milliseconds apart.
    -->
    <color name="swipey_window">#FBFBFD</color>

    <!--
      The ground behind the launcher icon's mark.

      White rather than the app's near-black canvas. The icon has to hold its own in a grid
      of other icons on a photograph, not match the screen it opens: a dark disc among the
      light ones every launcher is full of recedes into the wallpaper instead of reading,
      which is exactly what the first cut of this icon did.

      This one must NEVER gain a values-night counterpart. A launcher icon is a fixed piece
      of artwork: it keeps the same ground whether the phone is in light or dark mode, the
      same way every other icon on the home screen does. Give it a night override and the
      app's identity changes shape at sunset.
    -->
    <color name="swipey_icon_ground">#FFFFFF</color>
</resources>
